{:edb/db-before-t 2674 :edb/db-after-t 2675 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535987 50 #inst "2026-10-09T12:19:14.755Z" 13194139535987 true] [17592186161917 1020 #edb/ref 17592186378340 13194139535987 true] [17592186161917 1020 #edb/ref 17592186378347 13194139535987 true] [17592186161918 1020 #edb/ref 17592186378354 13194139535987 true] [17592186161919 1020 #edb/ref 17592186378361 13194139535987 true] [17592186162521 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535987 true] [17592186162521 1100 "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which of the following represents the corresponding quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,Ax$ in terms of the components of $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]?$" 13194139535987 true] [17592186162521 1100 "$A = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which of the following represents the corresponding quadratic form $x^{T}Ax$ in terms of the components of $x = \\begin{bmatrix}x_{1} \\\\ x_{2}\\end{bmatrix}$?" 13194139535987 false] [17592186162521 1145 "**Method 1**\n\nEach entry ${a}_{ij}$ of $A$ corresponds to the term ${a}_{ij}{x}_{i}{x}_{j}$ in the expression of the quadratic form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ax & =1{x}_{1}{x}_{1}+(-2){x}_{1}{x}_{2}+(-2){x}_{2}{x}_{1}+1{x}_{2}{x}_{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-2{x}_{2}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{1}^{2}-4{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo write down a quadratic form in terms of vector components, we compute the following expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ax & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2} \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={x}_{1}({x}_{1}-2{x}_{2})+{x}_{2}(-2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}) \\\\  & ={x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-2{x}_{2}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{1}^{2}-4{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535987 true] [17592186378340 1017 #edb/ref 17592186378341 13194139535987 true] [17592186378340 1089 "q-140929" 13194139535987 true] [17592186378340 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535987 true] [17592186378340 1100 "Consider the quadratic form \n$Q(x)={x}_{1}^{2}-4{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{3}-3{x}_{2}{x}_{3}.$ \nEvaluate $Q(x)$ when $x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139535987 true] [17592186378340 1113 #uuid "455cf0d5-7cc5-56d5-abef-02f0bf8e16a5" 13194139535987 true] [17592186378340 1145 "We are given that \n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the expression for $Q(x)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & ={x}_{1}^{2}-4{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{3}-3{x}_{2}{x}_{3} \\\\  & ={3}^{2}-4\\cdot 3\\cdot (-1)+2\\cdot 3\\cdot 0-3\\cdot (-1)\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =9+12+0+0 \\\\  & =21.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535987 true] [17592186378341 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378342 13194139535987 true] [17592186378341 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378343 13194139535987 true] [17592186378341 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378344 13194139535987 true] [17592186378341 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378345 13194139535987 true] [17592186378341 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378346 13194139535987 true] [17592186378341 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535987 true] [17592186378341 1041 "selection" 13194139535987 true] [17592186378341 1104 #edb/ref 17592186378342 13194139535987 true] [17592186378341 1110 #uuid "42760393-cb74-5f87-ad41-3056044a586b" 13194139535987 true] [17592186378342 1034 "21" 13194139535987 true] [17592186378342 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535987 true] [17592186378342 1111 #uuid "cdd64b22-569f-5869-b1a9-37782b5c26a7" 13194139535987 true] [17592186378343 1034 "6" 13194139535987 true] [17592186378343 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535987 true] [175